I'll note a data-quality issue first, then make the call.

Quick caveat: some CVE-to-service mappings here look off (e.g., CVE-2014-6271 is Shellshock/Bash, not Apache httpd itself; ProFTPD 1.3.3c's known issue is the backdoor CVE-2010-3867/OSVDB, and "CVE-2010-20103" doesn't match the classic ProFTPD backdoor). I'll prioritize based on realistic exploitability regardless.

